مایعات معدنی

Note: There are multiple possible translations depending on the context of the word ""πίσσα"". I provided 4 different options based on the most common interpretations of the word. 

* Πίσσα can refer to a type of resin or asphalt, in which case the Persian equivalent is ""مایعات معدنی"".
* Alternatively, it might refer to a sponge or an innocuous fluid, in which case ""اسفنج"" is a suitable translation.
* In a broader sense, πίσσα can describe something that is sacred or holy, in which case ""قدس"" is a fitting choice.
* Another possible translation is ""پودرآب"", which is a type of water-soluble adhesive."
